   (b) NO COMPETING FORKS. A fork published to continue maintenance,
       compatibility, or porting of a dormant project is permitted. A
       fork published to draw users away from the original project is
       not, whether by rebranding the Software, by removing or obscuring
       the credit required by 4(a), or by presenting the fork as an
       independent work rather than a continuation. If the original
       project resumes activity, you may continue to maintain and
       distribute your existing fork, but you must state on your
       distribution pages that the original project is active again and
       link to it.

   (c) NO RESALE. You may not sell the Software or derivative works of
